msgid "guard "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 0408:02AD"
msgid "Run, you fool! The Titans have been angered. No one is safe from their wrath. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 0408:033E"
msgid "Be off with you. There is no time for conversation when the walking dead march upon the city! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Goodbye. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 0408:03FE"
msgid "I told you to move along! Bother me with your questions later. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Hello, Tarna. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "What is your name? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "bark 0408:04B9"
msgid "Greetings, {name}."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 0408:04DB"
msgid "Greetings. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is your name? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:05F1"
msgid "I am Tarna, guardswoman of Tenebrae. Please tell me what it is you wish to know so that I might get on with my business. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is your name? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Tell me about your job. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is your name? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Tell me about Tenebrae. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hello, Tarna. " or "Hello. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Hello. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hello, Tarna. " or "Hello. "
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "bark 0408:0764"
msgid "You are, of course, staying out of trouble I trust, {name}."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hello, Tarna. " or "Hello. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:07B1"
msgid "You are, of course, staying out of trouble I trust. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hello, Tarna. " or "Hello. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:07FC"
msgid "Have you stopped me to chat or for more information? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hello, Tarna. " or "Hello. "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Information. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after ""
msgctxt "bark 0408:0889"
msgid "Waste not my time! If you have need to speak, then do so. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after ""
msgctxt "bark 0408:08AD"
msgid "Be off! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "A chat. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "A chat. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "A chat. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:0942"
msgid "I am sorry but I have not the time for such pleasantries. Good day. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Information. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:0A36"
msgid "I have no time to talk. Now that the Theurgists have lost their healing powers, the guards are on extra duty to insure no trouble breaks out. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Information. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:0ACD"
msgid "I am sorry, but with the change in rule, I am too busy dealing with Devon to answer your questions. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Information. "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Who is Orlok? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Information. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:0BE1"
msgid "I am sorry but I have not the time for such pleasantries. Good day. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Information. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:0CCE"
msgid "What information would you like? Surely by now you have seen enough of the city to have learned where everything is. Or was the Shattered Skull too busy for Orlok to tell you one of his tales? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who is Orlok? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:0E62"
msgid "Orlok is the bartender at the tavern. Though his stories are rather long on time and short on truth, they are quite entertaining. And, better yet, he fills his tankards to the top. However, watch how many you have. If you cause too much trouble, you might get thrown out -- if not by Jenna, then by me. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who is Orlok? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Who is Jenna? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where is the tavern? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Where is the tavern? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where is the tavern? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:0F60"
msgid "It is in the Southwest part of town. 'Tis hard to miss, it's such a large building. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who is Jenna? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:108C"
msgid "The barmaid? She is the daughter of the Captain of the Guard. She is feisty -- more like her father than he would care to admit. Judging the likes of you, she would come out the better in a fight. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me about Tenebrae. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:1202"
msgid "I suppose that should not be too difficult, since I have lived here my entire life. Some say Tenebrae does not need to be anything more than a bastion of security, since there is no other measure of civilization around, but I disagree. Give me my home and my blade and I'll protect her -- Tenebrae -- with my life. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me about Tenebrae. "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "No other measure? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Bastion of security from what? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Bastion of security from what? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Bastion of security from what? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:142F"
msgid "Well, initially, from the Zealans. That is why the city is divided into three sections. The rulers wanted addition defenses for the palace should the outer walls be breached.  Now, however, the walls are little more than divisions between the decent people and\tthe Necromancers. Not to, ah, imply that you or the Necromancers are -indecent- or any such thing, of course. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Bastion of security from what? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:1579"
msgid "Well, initially, from the Zealans. That is why the city is divided into three sections. The rulers wanted additional defenses for the palace should the outer walls be breached. Now, however, the walls are nothing more than divisions between the classes and boundaries for the weather... and the cemetery. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Bastion of security from what? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "What about the cemetery? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Zealans? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Zealans? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Zealans? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:17A8"
msgid "Indeed, you are a stranger not to know of the despicable Zealans. They are, or -were-, an insane collection of people who were too blind to recognize the power of the Titans. They foolishly and tenaciously held on to an archaic set of beliefs, and when the Titans demonstrated their might and authority, the Zealans refused to acknowledge the truth. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Zealans? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Boundary for the weather? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Boundary for the weather? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:19C4"
msgid "As long as we show proper reverence for The Lady Mordea, she shall bless us with skies of peace and calm. Cross her, however, and she shall call upon the might of Hydros, raining down upon the people a tempest the likes of which have never been felt before. Yet the Lady does not extend her kindness without the city walls, traveler beware. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about the cemetery? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:1AF9"
msgid "'Tis home to more than the dead it is. In accordance with our pact, we bring the lifeless corpses of our friends and brethren to the Necromancers there, and only they and Lithos know what happens after that. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about the cemetery? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Tell me about the Necromancers. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What pact? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "What pact? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What pact? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:1CB1"
msgid "Eons ago, our forebears formed a covenant with Lithos. He would cease his angry rumblings if we agreed to send our dead to him. There, deep in the heart of Pagan, the dead exist solely to serve the Mountain King's very wishes. And sometimes, Lithos has them wander the surface world as well! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What pact? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Wander up here? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Wander up here? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:1E37"
msgid "Aye, in the cemetery the undead wander, doing the bidding of the Necromancers, always ready to take the living down to the very depths of the Mountain King's domain. I would avoid the cemetery at all costs, I would.  Keep your business far from there. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "How do you send the dead? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "How do you send the dead? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "How do you send the dead? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:1EFB"
msgid "How in the blazes do you expect me to know? Burying them does it I suppose.  Why not ask a Necromancer? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me about the Necromancers. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:208F"
msgid "I'll tell you what I can. They say Necromancers deal with death. Well, I say that is not true -- Necromancers -are- death as far as I am concerned! I suppose someone must be responsible for maintaining our end of the pact, but how anyone can choose to do so willingly is beyond my comprehension. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "No other measure? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:2140"
msgid "Well, we've seen neither hide nor hair of another community, save the mages. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "No other measure? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "The mages? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "The mages? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:21CD"
msgid "Aye. The healers and the Sorcerers! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "The mages? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "What Sorcerers? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Describe the healers. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Describe the healers. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Describe the healers. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:23B7"
msgid "They call themselves Theurgists -- whatever -that- means. All I know is that they provide a valuable service to us here in the city, so I care not how it is done. I am grateful they do not require that we head to their home, Argentrock Isle, for such help. I consider it only too kind that the healers are willing to travel here. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Describe the healers. "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "How do the Theurgists arrive? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "How do the Theurgists arrive? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:2502"
msgid "A good question, that one, and one for which I have no answer. Rumor tells of magical devices that permit all the mages to teleport about Pagan, but I have seen no such thing, myself. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What Sorcerers? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:268F"
msgid "Ah, the black ones, followers of the Lord of Flame. The Necromancers may deal with death, but oft times I wonder whether the followers of Pyros are not the true representatives of evil. I do know this: Ask not too many questions of the Town Sorcerer, Beren, for our peace with him is tenuous at best. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me about your job. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:27C8"
msgid "I see. Very well, 'tis my lot to take care of my fellow Tenebraens, though I suspect that would include you as well, so long as you stay out of trouble. I keep the peace within and the war without, if you know what I mean. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me about your job. "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "What about the executions? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "The war without? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "The war without? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "The war without? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:2998"
msgid "Well, I suppose that would seem a bit obscure -now-. However, 'twas not that long ago when the Zealans still attempted to scale our walls. Of course, the raids actually ceased nearly a century ago, but defending the city from invaders is still an integral part of a guard's training! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "The war without? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "What are Zealans? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about the executions? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:2B0D"
msgid "They were part of maintaining order under Mordea's iron grip. I am glad there are fewer under Devon's rule. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about the executions? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:2B87"
msgid "What about them? They are a necessary part of maintaining order. Nothing more, but nothing less. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What are Zealans? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:2D1A"
msgid "Indeed, you are a stranger not to know of the despicable Zealans. They are, or -were-, an insane collection of people who were too blind to recognize the power of the Titans. They foolishly and tenaciously held on to an archaic set of beliefs, and when the Titans demonstrated their might and authority, the Zealans refused to acknowledge the truth. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Goodbye. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:2E68"
msgid "Halt! I have never seen you before, stranger. Identify yourself and your business in Tenebrae. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Goodbye. "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "What just happened here? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What just happened here? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:2FBA"
msgid "The execution is none of your business. Just be glad that a treasonous, despicable criminal has been properly punished. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What just happened here? "
msgctxt "bark 0408:30A9"
msgid "Now answer the question! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What just happened here? "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "I do not remember. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not remember. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:3148"
msgid "Well now, that's a little more like it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not remember. "
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "bark 0408:317F"
msgid "Well met, {name}."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not remember. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:31AF"
msgid "And where do you hail from? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not remember. "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Another world. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I come in peace. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "I come in peace. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I come in peace. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:32FD"
msgid "Well now, that's a little more like it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I come in peace. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:3374"
msgid "'Tis good to hear, stranger. I am certain that will not change. Do not prove me wrong, stranger. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I come in peace. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:33AF"
msgid "Now tell me, where do you hail from? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "My business, not yours. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "My business, not yours. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "My business, not yours. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:35C3"
msgid "If you truly believe that, then you are sadly mistaken. For every moment you spend in Tenebrae, what you are doing and where you are doing it is exactly my business as guard of the royal household! Now I repeat, state your name and business. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I said, not your concern! "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "I said, not your concern! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I said, not your concern! "
msgctxt "bark 0408:3736"
msgid "You won't last long here with an attitude like that. For the final time, will you tell me your name and business here in Tenebrae? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I said, not your concern! "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "No. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Yes. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "Yes. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Yes. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:37BE"
msgid "Well, what is it then? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "No. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:3841"
msgid "Then prepare to answer to my blade! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not remember. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:38C3"
msgid "Well now, that's a little more like it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not remember. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:395C"
msgid "Had a bit too much of Orlok's brew, eh? Well, you just watch yourself and stay out of trouble, and we'll have no quarrel with you. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not remember. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:3997"
msgid "Now tell me, where do you hail from? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "The beach. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "The beach. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "The beach. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:3B2F"
msgid "A fisherman, then? You do not dress like one who makes his living pulling nets from the sea. Then your business in the city is...? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "The beach. "
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "To make money. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "A place far away. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "A place far away. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "A place far away. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:3CCD"
msgid "Another island? I admit your clothing is unusual, but I was not aware there were other cities. Well, I suggest you quickly learn the laws and customs of -this- city. What is your business in the city? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Another world. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:3E97"
msgid "I may appear to be just a simple guard to you, but I outgrew such fairytales years ago. I suggest you change your tone with me or I will see your worthless hide resting on the inside of a jail! Now, if you would, tell me your business in the city. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not know. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "I do not know. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not know. "
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "bark 0408:401A"
msgid "Well you had best find out, {name}. We do not like trouble in the city."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not know. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:407D"
msgid "Well you had best find out, stranger. We do not like trouble in the city. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not know. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:4112"
msgid "You may go about your business. Please move along and do not disturb the widow until after I have escorted her from the docks. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "To return home. " or "To leave this place. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "To return home. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "To return home. " or "To leave this place. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0408"
msgid "To leave this place. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "To return home. " or "To leave this place. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:4240"
msgid "Then what in the Lady's name are you doing wandering around here? I suggest you quickly find your way. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "To return home. " or "To leave this place. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:42D5"
msgid "You may go about your business. Please move along and do not disturb the widow until after I have escorted her from the docks. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "To make money. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:43CB"
msgid "Whose business is not? While you are at it, buy yourself some better attire. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "To make money. "
msgctxt "bark 0408:4460"
msgid "You may go about your business. Please move along and do not disturb the widow until after I have escorted her from the docks. "
msgstr ""
